# papers/ — original-paper storage

Use one directory per paper. The directory name is the paper ID, for example
`MIT_18100B_2019F/`:

```text
papers/<PAPER_ID>/
├── paper.pdf      original paper, preserved unchanged
├── solution.pdf   official solution; without it the paper is practice-only
└── meta.md        problem-level register; fields are in exam_bank_spec.md §3
```

Rules:

- A paper directory not registered in `../index.md` produces a Doctor WARN.
- Missing `meta.md` columns or official-solution page references produce a WARN.
- Any assessment-pool paper/problem reference found in a lesson or exercise
  produces a FAIL, preserving assessment isolation.

The initial bank is empty. See `50_playbook/exam_bank_spec.md` §1 before adding
the first paper.

